# Deployment Targets

AWS CodeDeploy supports different deployment targets.

## 1. Amazon EC2 / On-Premises

CodeDeploy can deploy applications to:

- Amazon EC2 instances
- On-premises servers

For example:

```text
CodeDeploy
    ↓
EC2 Instance
    ↓
Application
```

This is useful for applications running on traditional servers.

---

## 2. AWS Lambda

CodeDeploy can also be used to control deployments of AWS Lambda functions.

For example:

```text
New Lambda Version
       ↓
CodeDeploy
       ↓
Lambda Function
```

This allows organizations to perform controlled Lambda deployments.

---

## 3. Amazon ECS

CodeDeploy can also be used with Amazon ECS for certain deployment strategies, particularly for **ECS services using blue/green deployments**.

Example:

```text
CodeDeploy
     ↓
Amazon ECS
     ↓
New Task Version
```

