# Deployment Lifecycle

During an EC2/on-premises deployment, CodeDeploy goes through different lifecycle events.

Some important lifecycle events include:

```text
ApplicationStop
      ↓
BeforeInstall
      ↓
Install
      ↓
AfterInstall
      ↓
ApplicationStart
      ↓
ValidateService
```

These lifecycle hooks allow you to execute custom scripts during deployment.

For example:

### ApplicationStop

Stops the currently running application.

### BeforeInstall

Performs tasks before the new version is installed.

### AfterInstall

Runs tasks after the new application files have been copied.

### ApplicationStart

Starts the new application version.

### ValidateService

Checks whether the application is running correctly after deployment.

